<title>USA: U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA rice export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Sales of 21,000 MT were up 55 percent from the previous week, but down 23 percent from the 4-week average.  Mexico (6,500 MT--all rough), the Netherlands (2,600 MT), the Netherlands Antilles (2,500 MT), Haiti (2,000 MT), Canada (1,600 MT), and Nicaragua (1,600 MT) were the primary buyers.</p>
<p>In addition, sales of 100 MT of rough rice were reported for Costa Rica.  Exports of 82,400 MT were two and two-thirds times the week earlier and two and nine-tenths times the 4-week average.  The major destinations were Costa Rica (26,600 MT), Turkey (20,900 MT), South Africa (9,000 MT), Haiti (4,800 MT), Mexico (3,800 MT), and the Netherlands (3,000 MT).</p>
</text>
